# 15. QR CODE — CUSTOMER ORDER ENTRY POINT
--------------------------------------------------

The QR Code is a CORE Phase 1 feature, not a placeholder.

The owner must be able to generate and view a QR code for the Food Cart's
customer ordering page.

Customer flow:

Owner Dashboard
    ↓
View QR Code
    ↓
QR Code generated from the Food Cart's unique customer URL
    ↓
Customer scans QR
    ↓
/order/[storeSlug]
    ↓
Customer Ordering Page

Example:

Store slug:
anna-street-food

Customer URL:

/order/anna-street-food

The QR code MUST encode the complete customer ordering URL.

DO NOT hardcode the QR code.

DO NOT use a static QR image.

The QR must be generated programmatically from:

base URL + store slug

Example:

https://<application-domain>/order/anna-street-food

For local development, it should automatically use the current application
origin so the QR points to the correct running application.

--------------------------------------------------
QR CODE UI
--------------------------------------------------

In the Owner Dashboard provide:

[ View QR Code ]

When clicked, open a polished modal containing:

- Food Cart name
- Short instruction:
  "Scan to order"
- Generated QR code
- Customer ordering URL
- Copy Link button
- Download QR button
- Print Poster button
- Close button

The QR must be scannable using a real mobile phone.

